<div class="adv-strip">Advertorial</div>

<article class="article">

  <h1 class="headline" id="headline">
    My dad smoked for 40 years. Now he's <em>190 days clean</em> — and going viral on TikTok.
  </h1>
  <p class="dek" id="dek">
    I'm a pharmacist. I built a lung supplement for the family I'd already lost. My dad is the one who got to use it.
  </p>

  <div class="byline">
    <span class="byline-avatar"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/dr-chris.jpg?v=1780079109" alt=""></span>
    <span>By <span class="byline-name"><b>Dr. Chris Jackson, PharmD</b></span></span>
  </div>

  <!-- HERO PHOTO -->
  <figure class="fig">
    <img id="hero-img" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/hero-tiktok-selfie.jpg?v=1780079113" alt="Dr. Chris Jackson and his dad Jack 'PawPaw' Jackson, arms around each other, smiling at the camera in the Betterbrand office — a neon TikTok logo glowing on the wall behind them.">
  </figure>

  <div class="body">

    <p>Hi. I'm Chris, and this is my dad ☝️</p>

    <p>I'm a Doctor of Pharmacy and a former Army combat medic, founder of <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Betterbrand</a> — and the son of a man you may have come across on TikTok recently.</p>

    <p>His handle is <strong>@real1jackson</strong>. We call him <strong>PawPaw</strong>. About six months ago, after more than 40 years of smoking, he decided he was done.</p>

    <!-- Viral pinned videos screenshot -->
    <figure class="fig viral-fig">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/viral-videos-trio.jpg?v=1780079112" alt="Three pinned TikTok videos from @real1jackson, including 'Day 12 Cigarette Free After 40 years Of smoking' at 313.2K views.">
    </figure>

    <p>He didn't tell anyone. He just stopped.</p>

    <p>Then, a few days later, with no real plan, he picked up his phone and made a TikTok. Then another one. Then another.</p>

    <p>He started at Day 1. Today he's at <strong>Day 190</strong>. And the internet won't stop watching.</p>

    <!-- Real TikTok comments — upside-down pyramid stack -->
    <aside class="comments" aria-label="Real comments from PawPaw's TikTok videos">
      <div class="comments-stack">
        <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/comment-cindy.png?v=1780079109" alt="TikTok comment from cindychristian979: 'Im at day 6!! prayers needed.'">
        <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/comment-boomer.png?v=1780079109" alt="TikTok comment from Boomer: 'Day 5 after 45 years myself stay strong'">
        <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/comment-sixmonths.png?v=1780079109" alt="TikTok comment from user2591604607966: 'I'm at six months after fifty years' — with a reply from Jack (Creator): 'That's outstanding'.">
      </div>
    </aside>

    <p>In his Day 175 video, he laid out his three reasons for quitting...</p>

    <aside class="reasons" aria-label="PawPaw's three reasons for quitting">
      <p class="reasons-eyebrow">PawPaw, Day 175 · His three reasons</p>
      <ol class="reasons-list">
        <li>
          <h3><span class="reasons-num">1</span> His family.</h3>
          <p>He wants to be around for his grandkids and great-grandkids.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3><span class="reasons-num">2</span> The cost.</h3>
          <p>Cigarettes were 26 cents a pack when he served in the Army in Germany. They're nearly $11 a pack now.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3><span class="reasons-num">3</span> His health.</h3>
          <p>He's walking again. Finding new parks. Visiting communities he hadn't been to in years.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </aside>

    <p class="spacer">And then he said this, on camera...</p>

    <div class="pq">
      "I don't have that cloud above me anymore. When I was smoking, I didn't realize how much it was pushing people away from me. Now I do."
      <cite>— PawPaw, Day 175</cite>
    </div>

    <!-- PHOTO: Chris + PawPaw together -->
    <figure class="fig">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/pawpaw-chris-beach.jpg?v=1780079114" alt="Jack 'PawPaw' Jackson with his son Dr. Chris Jackson, arm around his shoulder, on a beach. Dr. Chris is holding a bag of BetterLungs Mullein Gummies.">
    </figure>

    <p>He made another video earlier in the series — much earlier — that I had to watch twice before I could keep working. He simply called it <em>"Apologies to My Children and My Grandchildren."</em></p>

    <p class="spacer">That's my dad.</p>

    <h2>Now I want to tell you why <em>this one</em> matters to me.</h2>

    <p>My dad served in the United States Army before I did. He bought his first pack of cigarettes overseas, in uniform, in Germany. <strong>26 cents.</strong></p>

    <p>That pack turned into <strong>40+ years</strong> of smoking.</p>

    <!-- Polaroid family album -->
    <figure class="fig polaroid-stack">
      <div class="poly-board" aria-label="Family-album photos of Jack Jackson over the years">
        <div class="poly poly-army">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-army-portrait.jpg?v=1780079113" alt="Young Jack Jackson in U.S. Army dress uniform, American flag behind him.">
          <span class="poly-cap">U.S. Army</span>
        </div>
        <div class="poly poly-tank">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-tank.jpg?v=1780079114" alt="Jack sitting atop an armored vehicle in a helmet and sunglasses, another soldier behind him.">
          <span class="poly-cap">Germany</span>
        </div>
        <div class="poly poly-truck">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-truck.jpg?v=1780079115" alt="Jack as a young man in overalls and a plaid shirt, leaning against a blue pickup truck.">
          <span class="poly-cap">Home from service</span>
        </div>
        <div class="poly poly-van">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-truck.jpg?v=1780079115" alt="Jack and a friend posing in front of a dark Chevrolet van, late 1970s.">
          <span class="poly-cap">The '70s</span>
        </div>
        <div class="poly poly-swim">
          <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-swim.jpg?v=1780079113" alt="Jack today — older, smiling, swimming with goggles on, head above the water.">
          <span class="poly-cap">30 years in</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>From the family album. Dad's been my hero for as long as I can remember.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>I grew up watching it. The cough in the morning. The pack in the truck console. The way the smell got into the upholstery, the curtains, the hugs goodnight. The way he'd step outside on holidays and stand alone in the yard.</p>

    <p>I watched him try to quit. More than once. <em>Many</em> more than once.</p>

    <p>I watched the work his chest was doing when it shouldn't have had to.</p>

    <!-- PHOTO: Chris testing dad's lung capacity -->
    <figure class="fig">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/spirometer-chris-jack.jpg?v=1780079114" alt="Dr. Chris Jackson holding a three-ball incentive spirometer up to his dad Jack, who is breathing into the mouthpiece.">
    </figure>

    <p>That is, honestly, why I became a pharmacist. I thought the medicine could fix it. I thought there had to be a protocol.</p>

    <p>The medicine helped. It helped a lot of people. But for my dad — and for a lot of the people I grew up around who were also lifelong smokers — it wasn't enough on its own.</p>

    <p>So in 2019, I started <strong>Betterbrand</strong>, and the first thing we built was a daily lung-support supplement called <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BetterLungs</a>.</p>

    <!-- PHOTO: real mullein plant — varies by product line -->
    <figure class="fig" data-product="gummies">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/mullein-plant_19b86766-68e9-4f45-8bd1-bbbb5380a624.jpg?v=1780079114" alt="A gummy bear held up against a hillside of mullein plants in bloom.">
    </figure>
    <figure class="fig" data-product="bundle">
      <img src="{{ 'drchris-mullein-drops.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A bottle of BetterLungs Mullein + Chlorophyll drops held up against a hillside of mullein plants in bloom.">
    </figure>

    <p>It's built around <strong>mullein leaf</strong> — an herb people have leaned on for respiratory comfort since Greek and Roman times — dosed and tested by a pharmacist. We've made BetterLungs in a few different formats over the years: gummies, drops, and a nasal Reset Stick.</p>

    <p data-product="gummies">The newest one is a <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pear-flavored gummy</a>. And yes, my dad has a bag of them on his counter.</p>
    <p data-product="bundle">For my dad, the daily setup is our <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/quit-smoking-support-bundle?variant=51598663221547" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Quit Smoking Support Bundle</a> — Mullein + Chlorophyll drops paired with our nasal Reset Sticks. The drops live next to his coffee. A Reset Stick rides in his pocket for when the urge hits.</p>

    <p data-product="gummies">
      <a class="inline-cta" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See what PawPaw takes</a>
    </p>
    <p data-product="bundle">
      <a class="inline-cta" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/quit-smoking-support-bundle?variant=51598663221547" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See what PawPaw takes</a>
    </p>

    <p>Across the whole BetterLungs line, over <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>836,000 people</strong></a> have ordered one.</p>

    <p class="spacer">But I didn't build it for them. I built it for the man in those old photos. The one who tried, and tried, and tried.</p>

    <h2>And then, at Day 190, <em>he did it.</em></h2>

    <!-- PHOTO: Jack holding the product — varies by product line -->
    <figure class="fig" data-product="gummies">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0243/3030/5622/files/jack-holding-gummies.jpg?v=1780079112" alt="Jack 'PawPaw' Jackson smiling, holding up a bag of BetterLungs Mullein Gummies. Behind him, a red brick wall painted with the words 'WILLIE NELSON'.">
    </figure>
    <figure class="fig" data-product="bundle">
      <img src="{{ 'drchris-pawpaw-bundle.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Jack 'PawPaw' Jackson smiling, holding up a BetterLungs nasal Reset Stick and a bottle of Mullein + Chlorophyll drops. Behind him, a red brick wall painted with the words 'WILLIE NELSON'.">
    </figure>

    <p>He made it to <strong>Day 190</strong>. He's walking new trails, finding new parks, and breathing without a cloud above him — and honestly, I couldn't be prouder. If you have someone in your life who smokes, or is trying to quit, <a class="product-link" href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/collections/lung-detox-supplements/products/betterlungs-r-mullein-gummies?variant=50211146957099" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this is who I built BetterLungs for</a>, now.</p>
  </div>

